cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TREVIDEON in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TREVIDEON: TRemor Eulerian VIDEO magnificatiON"
abstract: >-
  Open-source tool for identifying and quantifying hand tremor from video. It magnifies sub-pixel tremor with
  phase-based Eulerian Video Magnification (Riesz pyramid), measures it with dense optical flow on the
  un-magnified video (frequency, amplitude, band power, spectra, envelopes), optionally isolates the dominant
  hand with a wrist-anchored, size-normalised view, repairs repeated video frames, and computes tremor
  statistics for user-defined event markers.
